From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rohan Raja <roraja@microsoft.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 17:05:32 -0700
Subject: Bound Windows clipboard/drag text reads by HGLOBAL GlobalSize

The Windows clipboard/drag readers in clipboard_util_win.cc built
strings directly from a locked HGLOBAL pointer (data.data()) and passed
it to string / UTF constructors that NUL-scan to find the end. An
untrusted IDataObject payload that omits a NUL terminator therefore
drives the scan past the allocation, leaking adjacent browser-process
heap to a web page (CWE-125- out-of-bounds read).

Treat GlobalSize() as authoritative: bound every text/URL/filename read
by data.size() and truncate at the first embedded NUL, mirroring the
already hardened CF_HTML path. Two centralized helpers,
HGlobalAsWideString and HGlobalAsString, cover the six text/URL sites
(handling the byte->char width conversion and the null-lock check); the
four filename sites are bounded inline.

Bug: 520521197
